Title: CLIMATE ANTHOLOGY: SEGMENT III - DROUGHT
Credit: Written by
Author: Screenwriting Class Collective
Draft date: October 2026
Format: Fountain

/* =========================================================================
   SEGMENT III: DROUGHT
   Setting: Dried alluvial river basin / Agricultural boundary town
   Themes: Hydrological failure, aquifer collapse, Day Zero rationing, food security.
   Atmospheric Context: 42°C, Relentless UV radiation, 0% Precipitation for 180 days.
   ========================================================================= */

EXT. RIVERBED BASIN - DAY

Where a quarter-mile-wide river flowed five years ago, there is now only an ocean of cracked, hexagonal mud tiles.

Two rusted iron navigation buoys sit stranded in the powdery silt, tilted at forty-five-degree angles like graveyard headstones.

MATEO (60), gaunt, arms corded with lean muscle, walks along what was once the central channel. He carries an iron probe rod and a digital groundwater acoustic sensor.

He drives the steel rod into the dried river sediment. 

THUD. Solid stone and packed clay. Not a hint of dampness.

MATEO
(to himself)
Eighty meters down. Nothing. The subterranean flow has stopped.

In the distance, the white carcass of a stranded river barge has been stripped down to its rusted steel ribs by scavengers.

EXT. MUNICIPAL WATER DEPOT - OUTSKIRTS OF TOWN - MIDDAY

The heat waves distort the horizon into shimmering liquid mirrors.

A line of three hundred people stretches along the chain-link fence of the regional reservoir pumping station. 

Almost everyone holds identical 20-liter blue plastic jerry cans. 

At the front of the line, two MILITARY POLICE OFFICERS in sweat-soaked tactical vests guard a single brass manifold with four spigots.

A hand-painted plywood sign reads:
**RATION ALLOCATION: 12 LITERS PER HOUSEHOLD PER 48 HOURS. TOKENS ONLY.**

SOFIA (28), holding a sleeping toddler on her hip and clutching two blue plastic cards, steps to the spigot.

CORPORAL DIAZ
Card.

Sofia hands him the token. Diaz swipes it across a handheld terminal. The terminal BEEPS twice with a sharp, red flash.

CORPORAL DIAZ (CONT'D)
Your quadrant exceeded allocation on Tuesday.

SOFIA
That was for the communal clinic. The sterilization autoclave needed distilled water. My children haven't had clean drinking water since yesterday morning.

CORPORAL DIAZ
The terminal locks out overrides, ma'am. Next in line!

SOFIA
(standing firm, voice trembling)
Look at the river! There is no next week! If you don't turn that valve, we won't be here next week!

The crowd behind Sofia murmurs. The murmur swells into a low, collective roar.

[[WRITING PROMPT FOR CLASSMATES: Mateo discovers an ancient perched aquifer under the limestone bluff, but it sits beneath disputed corporate farmland. Sofia must decide whether to lead a raid on the municipal reservoir valve station.]]
